{"id":549,"flavor":[{"games":["Legends: Arceus"],"text":"I suspect that its well-developed legs are the result of a life spent on mountains covered in deep snow. The scent it exudes from its flower crown heartens those in proximity."},{"games":["Shield"],"text":"Essential oils made from Lilligant flowers have a sublime scent, but they’re also staggeringly expensive."},{"games":["Sword"],"text":"It’s believed that even first-rate gardeners have a hard time getting the flower on a Lilligant’s head to bloom."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"It’s well liked by other Pokémon because of its beauty. The flower on its head needs constant care, or it will soon wither and rot."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"The fragrance of its flower differs slightly depending on the soil where it grew up. Sniffing the aroma calms your heart and mind."},{"games":["Moon"],"text":"As soon as it finds a male to be its partner, the beautiful flower on its head darkens, droops, and withers away."},{"games":["Sun"],"text":"No matter how much time and money is spent raising it, its flowers are the most beautiful when they bloom in the wild."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Y","Black"],"text":"Even veteran Trainers face a challenge in getting its beautiful flower to bloom. This Pokémon is popular with celebrities."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","X","White"],"text":"The fragrance of the garland on its head has a relaxing effect. It withers if a Trainer does not take good care of it."},{"games":["White 2","Black 2"],"text":"The fragrance of the garland on its head has a relaxing effect, but taking care of it is very difficult."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Chlorophyll","hidden":false,"description":"Boosts the Pokémon's Speed stat in harsh sunlight."},{"name":"Own Tempo","hidden":false,"description":"The Pokémon sticks to its own tempo, preventing it from becoming confused or being affected by Intimidate."},{"name":"Leaf Guard","hidden":true,"description":"Prevents status conditions in harsh sunlight."}],"eggGrou